            "number": 1,
            "title": "STATIC CMOS INVERTER CHARACTERIZATION",
            "date": "13/08/2026",
            "type": "main_experiment",
            "sections": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "number": 1,
                    "title": "AIM",
                    "text": "To design and simulate a static CMOS inverter using 180 nm technology and analyze its DC transfer characteristics and noise margins."
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "number": 2,
                    "title": "TOOL",
                    "text": "Cadence Virtuoso, Spectre Simulator, 180nm PDK."
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "number": 3,
                    "title": "THEORY",
                    "text": [
                        "The static CMOS inverter consists of a PMOS pull-up transistor and an NMOS pull-down transistor connected in series.",
                        "The switching threshold voltage $V_{TH}$ occurs at the point where $V_{in} = V_{out}$. Noise margins are given by $NM_H = V_{OH} - V_{IH}$ and $NM_L = V_{IL} - V_{OL}$."
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "table",
                    "number": 4,
                    "title": "DESIGN PARAMETERS",
                    "tables": [
                        {
                            "title": "CMOS Inverter Design Parameters",
